TC-CTBP5001-007
test scenario
Verify the receiving-jurisdiction effective-period check - the reporting fiscal year's start date falls within the jurisdiction's effective start/end dates -> included in the extraction scope
test data
"select IS_PARTNER from ctsg_enc.V_CTRY_PARTNER WHERE CTRY_CODE ='CA'
Set PTP_TAX_JRDT.OUT_DATE_STARTED <= start date of the Reporting Fiscal Year <= PTP_TAX_JRDT.OUT_DATE_ENDED (OUT_DATE_ENDED may also be NULL, meaning still open-ended)"
expected result
The element (General/Jurisdiction/Summary/UTPR) for that receiving jurisdiction should be included in the extraction scope

-- 1. Verify precondition: effective period of CA in the jurisdiction table
SELECT CTRY_CODE, OUT_DATE_STARTED, OUT_DATE_ENDED
FROM ptp_enc.TAX_JRDT
WHERE CTRY_CODE = 'CA';

-- 2. Verify the system treats CA as an active exchange partner
SELECT IS_PARTNER
FROM ctsg_enc.V_CTRY_PARTNER
WHERE CTRY_CODE = 'CA';

Test data condition: For CA, OUT_DATE_STARTED = 2025-01-01 and OUT_DATE_ENDED = 2027-12-30,
so the Reporting Fiscal Year start date (2025-01-01) falls within the effective period.

Query 1 returned CA with OUT_DATE_STARTED = 01-JAN-25 and OUT_DATE_ENDED = 30-DEC-27, which
covers the Reporting Fiscal Year start date (01-JAN-25). Query 2 returned IS_PARTNER = 'Y'.
Result matches expected. Pass.

CA's effective period covers the Reporting Fiscal Year start date, and IS_PARTNER = 'Y'.
